# THE SHIP: the players' flying magic ship (GameShip). RENDER ONLY: its collider is a kinematic body GameShip makes
# itself (the deck and the hull), and GameShip writes this entity's pose every frame. The origin is the deck top's
# centre; the bow points -Z. BLOCKY: 28 x 11 grid tiles (56 x 22 m; the middle line is x = 1). Models/airship.obj holds the pieces. THE WALL is
# not here: it is the ShipRail structures on the edge tiles (shipRail.pre), which can break.
# THE MAGIC: light crystals (gemsGlow's Diamond, unlit + Emissive: the bloom takes them) half in the hull - out of the
# second tier's sides, out of the stem, and a large one under the keel.
# Global: the game moves it, and it must be visited wherever it is. RootOnly: one cull entry for all the pieces.
# Mover: no shelter for the snow (the site map refreshes too slowly to follow it).
Prefab gameAirship
	Global true
	Mover true
	CullMode RootOnly
	Component Render
		ObjectContainer airship
		Node ShipHull
		Type StaticMesh
		Color 0.34 0.22 0.12
	Component Scene
		Entity
